cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "task-allocation-runtime: allocating decisions across people, language models and deterministic tools"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a task-analytic method for allocating the
  decisions in a cognitive task among deterministic tools, small language
  models, reasoning models and people. Task models follow an observe, orient,
  decide and act structure; an ordered allocation rule assigns each decision to
  a tier using formal specifiability, cognitive control, Cynefin domain and
  whether the decision is epistemic or normative. Machine tiers abstain and
  escalate, normative choices stay with people or explicitly scoped policies,
  and hand-offs to supervisors are typed and size-bounded. The repository also
  contains the protocol, code and synthetic materials of a completed
  computational study of the method on a synthetic air-to-air refuelling
  (tanker join) scenario. The Zenodo archive adds the study's collected
  records and analysis outputs.
